# AUDIT — ooda CLI zero-trust (power-law 20%)
File: ooda/audit/zero-trust.oot

Scope: this repo only. Date: 2026-09-03. Tag at audit: v2.11.0.
Doctrine: name is wrong until proven. Location is wrong until proven.
Content is wrong until a hostile probe fails closed then passes twice.

## 1. Verdict

The ooda binary is an argv router plus a ProcessCap shell around oodac.
Docs describe a 16-command product. The live wire is thinner and broken.
qa/ and scripts/ always print pass. CI auto-releases on push to main.
Do not trust any completion claim in this tree until probes execute.

The 20% that matters:
1. One argv contract (rest vs full) and one dispatch table in main.oo.
2. One compiler locator with one explicit token. No path chain.
3. Direct sys_exec of oodac. Kill sh -c.
4. Real qa probes that fail closed on the bugs below.
5. Kill dead files. Do not wrap them.

## 2. Kill list (dead code, no call site from main)

Kill, do not deprecate:

- build/args.oo — cli_build_args is never called. Duplicate of host_build parse.
- build/json_check.oo — run_check_json is never called.
- host_run.oo run_ooda_eval, run_ooda_repl — no main branch.
- host_build.oo cli_run_args — never called. run_oodac_run re-parses.
- fix/patch.oo — run_ooda_patch has no main branch.
- reproducible.oo run_build_reproducible — never called from host_build.
- reproducible.oo run_hermetic_landlock — never called. Also exec sh.
- json_check_version, log_stem, cli_bargs_has_repro — unused.
- token/cmd_extra.oo cmd_token_enforce_budget — superseded by v2; dead twin.
- qa/probe_*.oo — print a line and return Ok(0). Vacuous.
- scripts/{build,test,verify,release}.oo — print theater. Hardcode 0.1.0.

Docs that describe the dead wire are also dead: COMMANDS --hermetic,
--verify-reproducible, mcp-merge as a top-level command, VERSION file.

## 3. Argv contract split (P0 — Red 3)

Documented contract (docs/dispatch.oot): main slices rest; handlers never
see the subcommand name. main.oo does pass rest.

Handlers that index as if args[0] is still the subcommand (start at 1):

- build/test.oo, bench.oo, context.oo, gen.oo
- fix/digest.oo
- token/cmd_token.oo (sub = args[1]; len < 2 prints help)

Handlers that walk from 0 (correct for rest): fix.oo, fmt.oo, host_build
run_oodac_build, install.oo.

Predicted fail-closed bugs (write probes first):
- `ooda token status` prints help.
- `ooda test f.oo` misses the file.
- `ooda gen module User` prints usage.
- `ooda digest f.oo` misses the file.
- `ooda bench f.oo` misses the file.
- `ooda context src` ignores src.

Pick one contract. Kill the other. Rest is the documented one.

## 4. Fallbacks and compat to kill (P0 — Red 4)

- main.oo spawn: $OODACODEX/bin then $PATH. PATH is ambient.
- main.oo spawn: env_has/env_get/path_exists with no &EnvCap/&FsReadCap.
- host_run.oo: sys_exec(proc, "sh", "-c", cmd). Shell is ambient authority.
- fix.oo: two sh -c TTY probes. Same.
- install.oo: env_or fallback; oodac_bin OR bin/oodac; hardlink OR copy;
  alias `oo`; copies `runtime` not oodar; chmod/test via sys_exec;
  default OODA_VERSION v2.11.0.
- find_compiler.oo: claims no fallback; tries OODA_COMPILER, bin/oodac,
  ooda/oodac_bin. Docs claim OODA_HOME/oodac/oodac. Neither matches polyrepo.
- health.oo: probes ./oodac/oodac (monorepo path). Always prints ok.
- init.oo: writes CLAUDE.md, .cursorrules, .windsurfrules (compat editors).
  min_pin=v0.210.0. Banned .md except root README.
- apply.oo: HttpCap, FsCap (not in NORTHSTAR 14). Misses Process/Gpu/Ffi.

No mitigations. Old path dies.

## 5. Name vs function (first principles)

| File | Name claims | File does |
|---|---|---|
| build/ | build cluster | also init, gen, health, context, install |
| find_compiler.oo | no ambient fallback | three-path chain + wrong paths |
| health.oo | liveness of ooda | always ok; probes dead oodac path |
| context.oo | list .oo or stream codex | reads openOODA/LLMS.oot (deleted board) |
| digest.oo | lives under fix/ | sha256; not a fix |
| cmd_more.oo, cmd_extra.oo | extra/more | overflow dumps (banned generic) |
| cmd_tail.oo | tail/stream | one-shot full-file parse (residual) |
| cmd_ask.oo, cmd_query.oo | live ledger | canned 0 values (Red 3 stub) |
| docs/CLI_SETUP.oot | Editor Setup | install + caps + env |
| examples/build.oot | --out --emit c | live flags are -o --target |
| scripts/build.oo | compile the binary | prints "Compiling" |
| fmt/fmt.oo | Academy header | marketing title; 4-space indent |

ANCHOR.oo still lists VERSION. No VERSION file (RFC-0006). Keep it gone.

.github/workflows has no ANCHOR.oo. Either add one or do not treat
.github as a product dir.

build/ANCHOR.oo says "8 sub-files". The dir has 13 .oo files besides ANCHOR.

token/ANCHOR vs COMMANDS.oot vs cmd_token.oo disagree on the subcommand set.

## 6. Ocaps

NORTHSTAR 14 tokens. This binary takes 8 at main and does not attenuate
per branch (docs admit this). Gaps:

- spawn uses env and fs with no cap parameters (ambient).
- SysCap and BindCap are unused in the body.
- fmt.oo: AllocCap in signature; rewrite does not use the alloc param.
- token writes sidecars with FsWriteCap; audit/query/ask claim FsCap
  (legacy name).
- fix classify is substring search on oodac text (Red 1 heuristic).
- Landlock in reproducible.oo runs after the compile, not before.

Fail closed: digest.oo returns void on missing file (no process_exit).
main.oo wraps void handlers in Ok(0) even when the child process_exit
never ran. Mixed Result vs process_exit is two error channels.

## 7. 8-gate veto (current)

| Gate | Result |
|---|---|
| e1 Heuristic | VETO. classify(), je_code(), refuse_cli --version word, ask_route keywords. |
| e2 Boundary | VETO. argv off-by-one; digest silent miss; gen path check after len check. |
| e3 Data-path | VETO. Dead args/json_check/repro/patch/eval; stub qa/scripts; token zeros. |
| e4 Hermetic | VETO. sh -c, PATH spawn, ambient env, XDG install, oo alias. |
| e5 Temporal | OPEN. No replay probe. test.oo names bins by now_ms (non-deterministic). |
| e6 Drag | OPEN. Duplicate parse_int x4; duplicate heatmap; token is the long tail. |
| e7 Semantic | VETO. Vacuous probes. No mutant. Contracts absent on CLI entries. |
| e8 Byzantine | OPEN. digest uses crypto_sha256_internal; no timing probe in this repo. |

Any one veto blocks a victory claim. Three gates already veto.

## 8. Power law: keep vs kill weight

Keep (the product): main.oo router, find_compiler (one token), host_run
direct exec, host_build parse+dispatch, test, health (honest), fmt.

Kill or move out of this repo: token/* long tail (12 files of ledger
theater that live in std/compile/token_opt), gen/init editor scaffolds,
install XDG pack (belongs in packaging/), dead files in §2.

token/ is ~30% of the .oo lines and ~0% of the live CLI value until
ingest/query read a real ledger. That is the 80% tail.

## 9. Blue ocean (NORTHSTAR-aligned, not more subcommands)

Do not grow token subcommands. Unique move: the ooda binary becomes the
capability-gated Observe-Orient-Decide-Act loop for one .oo file.

- Observe: health + context that read this tree, not deleted LLMS.oot.
- Orient: oodac check JSON as a typed diagnostic, not substring bags.
- Decide: fix applies one AST edit (needs oodac), not text surgery.
- Act: build/run/test via direct exec of one OODA_COMPILER token.

One name. One cap set per beat. Zero shell. Zero PATH. Zero PATH-shaped
compat. Spawn opm/lsp/mcp only with an explicit bin token, same as oodac.

## 10. Next five (in this repo, in this order)

1. Hostile probes in qa/ that fail on §3 argv bugs. Then fix the contract.
2. Kill §2 dead files. Update ANCHORs and docs to match remaining wire.
3. Replace sh -c with sys_exec(oodac, argv...). Kill PATH spawn fallback.
4. One compiler token: OODA_COMPILER only. Kill bin/oodac and ooda/oodac_bin.
5. Stop auto-release from implying tests ran. Wire scripts/test.oo to qa/.

Do not start token polish, init templates, or install redesign until 1-4
land. Do not leave this repo for std/ or oodac/ without asking.
